<http://data.silknow.org/object/39c51ae1-dc18-362f-b5de-edeae17780fd/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Woman’s petticoat of ivory silk taffeta, striped with a weft of silver strip and brocaded with floral sprigs in white, black, green and shades of pink.  It is made of 5 panels of  silk, with two partial widths at the back.  The panel at the centre front is edged with 1-¼ inch (3 cm) wide ribbon of silver thread, on the sides and hem.  There is a wide  box pleat at centre front, with side pleats and pleats on either side of the opening at centre back, bound with 1-inch (2.5 cm) wide linen tape.  There are no pocket  openings. The hem is faced with a 3-inch (7.5 cm) strip of coarse, unbleached linen."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/39c51ae1-dc18-362f-b5de-edeae17780fd> .

